dewey(7)

# NAME

dewey - the multi-tier Go library in purse-first: layout, naming and stability

# DESCRIPTION

*dewey* is the Go module _code.linenisgreat.com/purse-first/libs/dewey_ (directory _libs/dewey_ in the purse-first repository). It is a library of utility packages whose source tree is arranged so that the dependency graph can be read off the directory names. This page describes that arrangement, how packages are named and published, and how mature each part is. The tool that maintains the arrangement is *dagnabit*(1); the model behind it is in *dagnabit*(7).

The commands under _libs/dewey/cmd/_ are built as separate packages of the purse-first flake (see *purse-first-nix*(7)).

# MODULE LAYOUT

_internal/_
	The implementation. Every package lives at _internal/<level>/<leaf>_, where _<level>_ is a NATO phonetic level (see LEVELS) and _<leaf>_ is the package directory name. Go forbids importing _internal/_ from outside the module.

_pkgs/_
	The public surface. One generated facade package per exported leaf, at _pkgs/<leaf>_, re-exporting the symbols of the matching internal package. Consumers import _code.linenisgreat.com/purse-first/libs/dewey/pkgs/<leaf>_. The facades are generated by *dagnabit export* and carry a *Code generated by dagnabit* header; do not edit them by hand. See *dagnabit*(7), *FACADES*.

_cmd/_
	Binaries that belong to the module: the static analyzers (see *dewey-analyzers*(7)), the *mesa*(1) renderer and _reflexive-interface-generator_.

_gclplugin/_
	The golangci-lint module plugin that registers the analyzers; see *golangci-lint-dewey*(1).

_initsmoke/_ and _dagnabit.toml_
	Generated per-architecture blank-import tests and the configuration that drives them; see *dagnabit*(1), *init-smoke*.

# LEVELS

A package at a given level depends only on packages at strictly lower levels within the module. The levels present in _internal/_ are _0_, _alfa_, _bravo_, _charlie_, _delta_, _echo_, _foxtrot_ and _golf_. Levels are computed from the live import graph by *dagnabit*, not chosen by hand, so a package moves between level directories when its dependencies change. See *dagnabit*(7), *THE LEVEL RULE*.

# PACKAGE NAMING

Because levels change, documentation and conversation refer to a package by its _leaf_ only, written _\*/<leaf>_ (for example _\*/go\_list_). The level is deliberately a wildcard.

The convention requires leaf names to be unique across the whole tree, and requires every package to sit exactly at _<level>/<leaf>_ with no nested sub-packages. That is a convention, not yet a gate: the validators for it, _ValidateUniqueLeaves_ and _ValidateTwoLayerLayout_, are exported by the dagnabit package but are not called by any build step, linter or recipe in the repository (tracked as purse-first#210). Only *dagnabit rename* enforces both, as a precondition; *reposition*, *move* and *export* do not check leaf uniqueness. Keep leaf names unique by hand until that is wired.

# PUBLIC PACKAGES

_pkgs/_ holds one facade per exported leaf. The ones that matter for the topics covered by other pages are:

*analyzer\_actx*, *analyzer\_defererr*, *analyzer\_paramobj*, *analyzer\_repool*, *analyzer\_seqerror*, *analyzer\_testui*
	The static analyzers; see *dewey-analyzers*(7).

*command*, *cli*, *config\_cli*, *flag\_policy*, *flags*, *output*, *ui*, *operation\_viewport*
	CLI-application scaffolding; see *dewey-cli*(7).

*mesa*
	The list-table renderer and NDJSON row protocol behind *mesa*(1).

*dagnabit*, *go\_list*, *go\_module*, *nato\_levels*, *topological\_sort*
	The primitives *dagnabit*(1) is built from.

# STABILITY

The maintainers' notes in _libs/dewey/CLAUDE.md_ classify packages by maturity. This page repeats that classification; it is a statement of intent by the maintainers, not something checked by the build.

Battle-tested
	*dagnabit*, *go\_list*, *go\_module*, *nato\_levels*, *topological\_sort*.

Experimental (treat the interface as a contract in flux)
	*command*, *cargo\_workspace*, *cargo\_manifest*, *cargo\_metadata*, *dagnabit\_rust*, *mesa*.

Packages not named in either list have no recorded classification.

# TESTING

The module is tested with the *test* build tag set (*go test -tags test ./libs/dewey/...*, wrapped by the repository's _test-dewey_ recipe). According to _libs/dewey/CLAUDE.md_ the tag gates helpers that must not ship to consumers. In _internal/_ a *go:build* constraint mentioning the tag appears in the *test\_ui*, *ui* and *pivy* packages.

# SEE ALSO

*dagnabit*(7), *dewey-analyzers*(7), *dewey-cli*(7), *purse-first-nix*(7), *dagnabit*(1), *golangci-lint-dewey*(1), *mesa*(1), *purse-first*(1)
